o 10,11,12 — upward. Yes. Our original path from left point A ... sweep 1 goes up then right then down to left. That's correct for far phase (left arm when crank rotating, goes up). For relative, center = (38,0), start at (0,0), arc to (76,0) sweep 1 (via top). Then to (0,0) via bottom. Path:\n`M 0 0 A 38 38 0 1 1 76 0 A 38 38 0 1 1 0 0`. Good.\n\nNear foot base translate 528,455, center relative (-38,0), path `M 0 0 A 38 38 0 1 1 -76 0 A 38 38 0 1 1 0 0`, start at right of center angle 0, sweep=1 goes down then left etc. Good.\n\nBut nested group animateMotion with path coordinates: parent transform translate; local user coords shifted. Yes.\n\nIn static, feet at base. Great. Add base d. Then preview legs/feet.\n\nNeed add feet perhaps not hidden. Near leg path orange. The near leg at phase 0 from (462,306) Q(514,380) to (528,455) appears through bottom. The far leg darker from 432 to 452. The far leg might be behind frame, but visible under top tube. Good.\n\nAlso consider body sits lower? Hip starts 306 inside body bottom edge. Fine.\n\nFix."}
