{"type":"thinking","text":"Let's design replacement scarf paths. Need ensure path layering. Red scarf tails below neck, over body. We can put a ribbon with cream stripe and fringe. We'll maintain rotation around knot 528,233.\n\nPath upper:\n```\n<path d=\"M 529 222\n C 493 207 463 216 433 207\n C 405 198 380 203 353 194\n L 345 207\n L 326 209\n L 346 219\n C 376 229 407 226 438 234\n C 468 242 501 244 529 238 Z\" fill=\"#d95545\" stroke=\"#a93d31\"...>\n```\nThis shape crosses body y 207-244, extends left. Add a cream stripe:\n`M 522 230 C 490 222 463 227 435 220 C 405 212 377 215 349 207` stroke #f3c56b width 4 maybe line along length. Follows.\nFolds:\n`M 505 219 C 478 217 456 221 430 214` etc.\nFringe at left end:\n`M 346 195 L 337 194 M 341 201 L 332 200 M 346 219 L 338 225` maybe. But end points not exactly. The end shape has points at (353,194),(345,207),(326,209),(346,219). The \"fringe\" could branch from x340 around y195, y202, y211. Add 3 thin strokes extending left 10px. That reads scarf. Need not overdo.\n\nLower tail:\n```\n<path d=\"M 529 234\n C 503 240 480 250 458 251\n L 453 261\n L 435 264\n L 454 271\n C 481 271 506 263 530 248 Z\" fill=\"#c5483b\" .../>\n```\nEnd fringes at x435 etc. This lower tail is shorter vertical. Add stripe.\nMaybe overlap makes a two-tail scarf.\n\nAdd gold cream stripe width 3.5.\n\nBut do red tails look like feathers because pointed? With fringe and stripes, likely more fabric.\n\nCould make scarf pale yellow to contrast red helmet. Let's consider: Red scarf + red helmet is coordinated. A mustard scarf also matches sun. With beak orange, too much warm. Red it is.\n\nWing:\nMain shape should be less tubular. Use a broader trailing edge and feather lobes. Let's design precisely:\nMain path:\n`M 481 225 C 514 227 545 240 573 259 C 598 276 621 291 638 300 C 648 305 650 315 640 320 C 628 326 610 316 592 306 C 568 292 542 282 513 277 C 492 274 476 260 481 225 Z`\nSimilar. Thickness at mid x520: top ~235 lower ~274 => 39. At tip 638,320. Still long. Add layered feathers below.\nMaybe wing should be bent with a \"wrist\" at grip. Fine.\n\nAdd a big scapular feather:\n```\n<path d=\"M 490 238 C 515 242 542 252 564 267 C 548 276 527 274 510 264 C 497 257 488 249 490 238 Z\" fill=\"#f0e4d1\" stroke=\"#cfc0a8\" .../>\n```\nThese layers add feathers.\n\nThen trailing edge feathers:\n```\n<path d=\"M 505 272 C 533 281 557 294 580 310 C 566 313 552 308 540 301 C 525 292 512 284 505 272 Z\" fill=\"#f8f1e4\" stroke=\"#cdbda5\" .../>\n<path d=\"M 535 284 C 558 294 578 306 595 321 C 582 324 569 319 558 311 C 546 303 537 294 535 284 Z\" .../>\n```\nThese extend below main wing edge, making feathered.\n\nPrimary fan at tip (slate):\n1. `M 599 289 C 617 289 636 296 650 306 C 639 311 626 309 614 303 C 606 299 600 294 599 289 Z`\n2. `M 592 299 C 608 304 623 312 635 323 C 624 326 612 321 603 314 C 596 309 592 304 592 299 Z`\n3. `M 583 307 C 598 315 610 323 619 334 C 608 336 598 330 590 323 C 585 318 582 312 583 307 Z`\n4. Maybe top white covert over primaries:\n`<path d=\"M 597 286 C 617 288 636 296 651 306 C 643 301 628 294 614 291 C 607 290 601 288 597 286 Z\" fill=\"#f6ecdc\"/>`\nThen feather shaft highlights on each:\n`M 607 293 C 622 298 636 304 647 310` etc.\nThese fan down/back, but their ends at x650, y306; x635,323; x619,334. Handlebar is x656,y307 to 639,327. They cross the bar. At the right, the handlebar grip maybe behind. Fan appears to grip.\n\nBut the primaries might look like a teal fan of feathers, much better than mitten. Add a little cream wing \"thumb\" around the bar? Not needed.\n\nWing main shape should connect to primaries; yes at 638,320, overlapping base.\n\nAlso add one small shoulder arc.\n\nThe bot's wing still long but feathery.\n\nShould the wing be drawn before the neck? Currently scarf, neck, wing, head. Wing is after neck, so overlaps neck bottom? It starts at 481,225 and scarf at 528, so maybe wing covers scarf knot! In crop, the wing starts below knot and the red knot at neck visible above? The knot is drawn later after head, so it's on top. Good. The wing partly covers scarf tails at 500? The tails at 500,240 might be covered by wing, that's okay. Scarf shapes still visible left.\n\nNeed perhaps move knot to 524,235. Fine.\n\nLet's edit."}
